@AC 1112. Those who have... obtained thence a conscience and life of charity.

@TCR 532[end]. The seeds implanted by the Lord obtain a free soil.

@SE 4039. Those who have obtained a conscience...

Obtain.; Potiri. @HH 6[end].

Obvious. See <"Meet, To"-Obviam>.

Occasion.; Occasio.
Occasional.; Occasionalis.
