@DP 101. These are they who omit to think concerning evil; and, as they omit it, they are continually in it. @278.

@AR 82[end]. He then... omits the goods of charity.

@108[end]. As they omit or hold cheap the truths of doctrine...

@AE 374[6]. "He passed them over, and did not kill them" (Jeremiah 41:8) = that they were not profane, thus not damned.

Omit.; Supersedere.

@AC 4402[3]. (Therefore) the opening of these things cannot be dispensed with.

@HH 553[3]. The mention of which I omit.

@AR 44. I forbear from confirming it further.

